{
	"name": "LiveConnect 08 — Incoming Messages with Proxy Trigger",
	"nodes": [
		{
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Receiving proxy messages with the native trigger\n\nThe **LiveConnect Proxy Trigger** (v0.2.0+) automatically registers the channel webhook when you activate the workflow, and removes it when you deactivate it. No manual webhook setup needed.\n\n**Configure:**\n1. `Channel Name or ID`: the channel to listen to (`Channel · Get Many`).\n2. `Secret`: leave it empty — it is generated and validated automatically.\n3. Activate the workflow (the registration happens at that moment).\n\n⚠️ One webhook per channel: do not activate two workflows with the same channel.\n\nThe exact payload of the proxy notifications can vary: run a real test and adjust the IF/response to whatever arrives (the trigger always delivers `raw`).",
				"height": 380,
				"width": 460
			},
			"id": "b8000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
			"name": "Instructions",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [
				0,
				-240
			]
		},
		{
			"parameters": {
				"id_canal": "",
				"secret": "",
				"simple": true,
				"path": "proxy-mensajes"
			},
			"id": "b8000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
			"name": "LiveConnect Proxy Trigger",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-liveconnect.liveConnectProxyTrigger",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [
				540,
				60
			]
		},
		{
			"parameters": {
				"conditions": {
					"options": {
						"caseSensitive": true,
						"leftValue": "",
						"typeValidation": "loose",
						"version": 2
					},
					"conditions": [
						{
							"leftValue": "={{ $json.mensaje }}",
							"rightValue": "",
							"operator": {
